# Pairs with RNoStrandedPrepare, and reproduces issue #4508, the residual of
# #4482's intended fix. The fix is applied: the export ships a decision row for
# every saga the origin still stores, an aged-out one resolved by its recorded
# verdict, and the receiver's prepare seam dedupes against it - materialised
# on Committed, dropped on Aborted, staged only while the saga is undecided.
# Pre-cut records are still re-shipped. What remains is a saga whose decision
# row the origin has already PURGED: the export carries no verdict for it, the
# receiver has nothing to dedupe against, and a retained prepare whose terminal
# was trimmed is staged with no terminal behind it. With the purged branch
# removed (snap0 for a forgotten saga is its recorded verdict only) the same
# change is clean on every property.
MODULE: RNoStrandedPrepareDedupeOverPurgedDecision
TARGET: RNoStrandedPrepare
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: with the #4482 dedupe in place, a pre-cut prepare re-shipped for a saga whose decision the origin purged is still staged with no terminal
PERTURBS: Bootstrap, DeliverPrepare

--- FIND
    /\ \E snap \in Snap0 :
         /\ rproj' = [k \in XKeys |-> ExportRow(snap, k)]
         /\ rpend' = [k \in XKeys |-> IF ExportsPrepared(snap, k) THEN "pending" ELSE "none"]
    /\ outbox' = {}
    /\ rconn' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, dlv, rterm, registryVars, barrierVars>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ \E snap \in Snap0 :
         /\ rproj' = [k \in XKeys |-> ExportRow(snap, k)]
         /\ rpend' = [k \in XKeys |-> IF ExportsPrepared(snap, k) THEN "pending" ELSE "none"]
\* MUTATION: the export's decision row is recorded on the receiver.
         /\ rdec' = [rdec EXCEPT !["A"] = IF snap \in {"committed", "aborted"} THEN snap ELSE rdec["A"]]
\* MUTATION: any pre-cut record still retained is shipped again.
    /\ outbox' \in SUBSET outbox
    /\ rconn' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, dlv, rterm, rarr, rexp, rout, rstage, rdeleg, rdial, barrierVars>>
--- END
--- FIND
    /\ rpend' = IF rterm[m.key] = "none" THEN [rpend EXCEPT ![m.key] = "pending"] ELSE rpend
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, rconn, rterm, rproj, registryVars, barrierVars>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a prepare is deduped by txid against the recorded decision.
    /\ rpend' = IF rterm[m.key] = "none" /\ rdec[TreeOf(m.key)] = "inflight" THEN [rpend EXCEPT ![m.key] = "pending"] ELSE rpend
    /\ rproj' = IF rdec[TreeOf(m.key)] = "committed" THEN [rproj EXCEPT ![m.key] = "post"] ELSE rproj
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, rconn, rterm, registryVars, barrierVars>>
--- END
--- FIND
    IF forgotten[T] THEN {"indeterminate", "inflight"} ELSE {Origin!RegistryView(T)}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a stored aged-out row exports its recorded verdict; a purged one exports nothing.
    IF forgotten[T] THEN {decision[T], "inflight"} ELSE {Origin!RegistryView(T)}
--- END
